      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b27551c_a85de759",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-04T19:59:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think override is the correct term here. In a way there are 2 things being controlled.\n\n1) override is on/off\n2) if override is on, then request 2 or 4 lane mode",
      "parentUuid": "04221e94_69f340a3",
      "revId": "1828d502815afe107ed3d5009d71a6de1c584726",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ad5c543_a516b33b",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-07T17:31:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Buried in L207 return from `int pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode()` is an implicit policy/logic decision. Perhaps this policy could be made more explicit or pulled out/exposed.\n\n\u003e return 1 \u003c\u003c get_next_bit(\u0026pin_caps);\n\nwherein `ec/common/util.c`\n\n\u003e * Get-and-clear next bit from mask.\n\u003e * Starts with most significant bit.\n\nPer DP AltMode v2.0 spec `Table 5-5: DP Capabilities (VDO in the Responder USB PD Discover Modes VDM)`, order MSB-\u003eLSB in caps is:\n\n* E (16)\n* D (8)\n* C (4)\n\nThus, even if MF_PREF is \u0027masked/forced to 0\u0027, we are implicitly biased towards selecting PinD. (Since D is sandwiched between C and E, note a following operation masks/hides E if C|D present. Elevating D.)\n\nI think that buried logic confounds the spirit of this CL a bit.\n\nAs commented in Bug, for reliable behavior in-vivo, we need a \u0027mask/force-off\u0027 for both MF_PREF (the policy bit, currently this) and MODE_DP_PIN_MF_MASK (the pin configs for Multifunction, currently absent).\n\nWarning:\n\nPlease note while PinC is *always* required per spec, some noncompliant docks exist that only advertise PinD (without accompanying PinC). Whatever masking logic used must be robust to this ecosystem bug.",
      "parentUuid": "2b27551c_a85de759",
      "revId": "1828d502815afe107ed3d5009d71a6de1c584726",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22c7964f_d842ede9",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-07T17:38:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was in error: MF_PREF being set to 0 should mask/hide any MF pins.\n\nIt is only if MF_PREF being 1 will the MSB logic trigger.\n\nWhich in turn, in buggy DUT, will fall through to PinC.\n\nThe only bug I can envision is a MF\u003d0,Pin\u003dD dock. This would not function.",
      "parentUuid": "1ad5c543_a516b33b",
      "revId": "1828d502815afe107ed3d5009d71a6de1c584726",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4dd0d216_f751b521",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1153746
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-07T18:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mfoverride on --\u003e we ignore MF bit and we ask for assignment C\nmfoverride off --\u003e we honor MF bit and we ask assignment C or D.\n\nNathan the case you were mentioning, is when 2-lanes of DP connected in the dock and USB 2 lanes are not connected correct?",
      "parentUuid": "2b27551c_a85de759",
      "revId": "1828d502815afe107ed3d5009d71a6de1c584726",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
